    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. `AcceptanceTest` is the only executable test class in the project (the other two files are support/base classes), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule \u2014 `membershipTier` becomes `'GOLD'` when the owner's household has 3+ members after the create \u2014 keeping each piece of logic in its proper place:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`): Added a persisted `householdSize` field (column `household_size`) with accessors, mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern. Updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `\"GOLD\"` first when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE rules. The tier stays a pure derivation of the owner's own fields, so a fresh `getOwner` read reflects it.\n\n2. **`HouseholdRegistrar.register`** (`rest/assignment/HouseholdRegistrar.java`): Changed it to return the post-create household member count, computed within its *existing* single pass over owners (counting the joining owner plus every key-matched housemate). Because the registrar already back-fills the shared `householdId` onto all same-lastName+address owners, counting by household key is exactly \"owners sharing the same householdId after this create.\" No extra query, no double-save.\n\n3. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`): Stamps `owner.setHouseholdSize(...)` from the registrar's return value, right next to the existing `namesakeCount` assignment.\n\n4. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`): Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (which generates `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`) and updated its description \u2014 without this the mapper threw `No enum constant ... GOLD`.\n\n5. **Schema files**: Added `household_size INTEGER` to the h2, hsqldb, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files.",
